# Shell scripts must keep LF line endings so they run on Linux and macOS
# regardless of the checkout platform's core.autocrlf setting.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The contract.tsv LF rule is NOT here. It lives in the repository-root
# .gitattributes, and putting it here instead is what went wrong once:
# packaging/buildsource.bat builds the source zip with
#
#     git archive --prefix=femm-qt/ HEAD        run from femm-qt/
#
# and that subtree archive does not apply this file. A rule written here
# therefore governs checkouts and stops governing the distribution, which is
# the half that reaches other machines -- every source zip shipped
# contract.tsv as CRLF while the committed blob was LF. See the root
# .gitattributes for the full account.
#
# The *.sh rule above is duplicated at the root and kept working throughout,
# which is precisely why the failure was invisible. Add new rules to the ROOT
# file unless they are meant to apply to checkouts only.
